# Model per provider and tier, picked by the parent session's $PI_PROVIDER.
# Profiles set `tier:`; a provider/tier with no row falls back to the parent's
# model. Add a provider by adding four rows. When new model versions ship, run
# `pi-subagent tiers` to see them and `pi-subagent tiers --update` to apply.
#
# fast      cheapest capable model, low thinking: recon, lookups, mechanical edits
# standard  mid-tier, medium thinking: most well-scoped delegations
# deep      top reasoning, high thinking: hard tasks with explicit completion criteria
#           (loops on vague goals, so keep it off open-ended work)
# intent    reads human intent and makes judgment calls: scoping, UX, product tradeoffs
#
# provider      tier      model[:thinking]
anthropic       fast      anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5:low
anthropic       standard  anthropic/claude-sonnet-5-5:medium
anthropic       deep      anthropic/claude-opus-5-5:high
anthropic       intent    anthropic/claude-fable-5-1:medium
openai-codex    fast      openai-codex/gpt-6-luna:low
openai-codex    standard  openai-codex/gpt-6-luna:max
openai-codex    deep      openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:high
openai-codex    intent    openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium
